# tests/jsfb/NARROW -- the implementations this browser is measured against when
# the question is "does a MAINSTREAM framework run", rather than "does the
# platform hold" (which is what tests/jsfb/BASELINE's 30 build-free rows ask).
#
# WHY A SECOND LIST EXISTS AT ALL, since a list of names is the thing this tree
# distrusts. tests/jsfb/BASELINE is taken over the 30 implementations that need
# no npm build, and jsfb_matrix.py says why that row set is fixed: "Letting a
# build change the ROW SET of a change detector would mean the baseline records
# the state of a working directory rather than the state of the browser."  That
# is right for a change detector and it has a consequence nobody wrote down --
# NOT ONE MAINSTREAM FRAMEWORK IS IN THOSE 30.  The 15 implementations that pass
# all eight operations are five vanillajs variants, two wildflowerjs, bobril,
# plastron-dom, and five outputs of functional-language compilers.  React, Vue,
# Svelte, Angular, Solid, Preact, Lit, Qwik, Alpine, Ember, Mithril, Inferno,
# Stencil, Marko, Riot and Knockout have ZERO rows in it and have never been
# driven.
#
# NOTHING HERE MAY BE BRANCHED ON. This file names WHAT IS MEASURED; it is read
# by tests/unit/jsfb_buildnarrow.py, which builds them, and passed to
# jsfb_matrix.py's --only, which filters rows. No line of the browser sees a
# framework name, and the whole value of this corpus is that it cannot be fitted
# to: you cannot special-case 27 independent codebases into working, you can
# only implement the platform they all stand on.
#
# THE LAST FOUR ARE NOT TARGETS, THEY ARE THE APPARATUS CHECK. They are already
# recorded at 8/8 in tests/jsfb/BASELINE, they need no build, and they span the
# two authorship shapes the corpus is valuable for -- two hand-written
# (vanillajs, bobril) and two emitted by a compiler from PureScript and Haskell
# (halogen, reflex-dom). If any of the four stops passing, the apparatus moved
# and no other number taken in the same run is believable.

# --- React: the same library four ways, so a failure can be placed --------
keyed/react-hooks
keyed/react-classes
keyed/react-redux-hooks
keyed/react-compiler-hooks

# --- Vue, including the compiler that emits no virtual DOM (vapor) --------
keyed/vue
keyed/vue-jsx
keyed/vue-pinia
keyed/vue-vapor

# --- compile-to-DOM: no runtime diff at all -------------------------------
keyed/svelte
keyed/solid
keyed/solid-store

# --- Angular: zone-based change detection vs signals -----------------------
keyed/angular-cf
keyed/angular-cf-signals

# --- small-runtime VDOM ----------------------------------------------------
keyed/preact-hooks
keyed/preact-signals
keyed/inferno
keyed/mithril

# --- web components / templates -------------------------------------------
keyed/lit
keyed/stencil

# --- attribute-driven and observable-driven, no build-time template step ---
keyed/alpine
keyed/knockout
keyed/riot

# --- resumability and compile-to-string ------------------------------------
keyed/qwik
keyed/marko
keyed/astro
keyed/hono

# --- the one with its own module/build system ------------------------------
keyed/ember

# --- APPARATUS CHECK: already 8/8 in tests/jsfb/BASELINE, build-free --------
keyed/vanillajs
keyed/bobril
non-keyed/halogen
non-keyed/reflex-dom
